<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<openrocket version="1.11" creator="OpenRocket 26.xx-SNAPSHOT-5f164fd0e">
  <rocket>
    <name>Chute release</name>
    <id>740b548e-cfd3-41a6-b23c-142f461b4211</id>
    <axialoffset method="absolute">0.0</axialoffset>
    <position type="absolute">0.0</position>
    <comment>A simple model rocket example adapted to use an electronic chute release.

A Chute Release is a small electronic device that holds a parachute closed until it drops to a pre-selected altitude, intended for use on windy days and small fields when descent drift under a parachute needs to be limited.

This example assumes a 30 inch parachute. The chute release is modelled by using a drogue chute with the same CD as the main, sized to give a reasonable descent rate, and adjusting the size of the main chute so the total area of the drogue and main is the area of the main parachute.</comment>
    <designer>Sampo Niskanen, adapted by H. Craig Miller and Joe Pfeiffer</designer>
    <designtype>original</designtype>
    <revision>2023-10-10: replaced streamer with drogue chute and adjusted size of main chute.</revision>
    <motorconfiguration configid="95aac292-c018-4713-8660-bd1a4714a0c2">
      <stage number="0" active="true"/>
    </motorconfiguration>
    <motorconfiguration configid="3c6373fb-a84b-4dd3-8b84-bfc96c7233d5" default="true">
      <stage number="0" active="true"/>
    </motorconfiguration>
    <referencetype>maximum</referencetype>

